## Important implementation notes

- The ARM template no longer outputs `applicationInsightsName`, `staticWebAppName`, or `staticWebAppDefaultHostname`.
- The ARM template now outputs `sqlServerName`, `sqlDatabaseName`, and `sqlFirewallRuleName`.
- The Key Vault name uses `kv-nscs-sec-<suffix>` instead of `kv-nscs-platform-<suffix>` to stay inside the Azure Key Vault 24-character name limit.
- The two GitHub-hosted script filenames were intentionally preserved to avoid forcing you to change launcher URLs.
- If your lab instructions currently reference `Cloud Slice`, `investigation-artifacts`, `business-files`, or `web-content`, update those references to the new NSCS names.

## SQL ARM integration

SQL is now deployed by `azuredeploy-nscs-storage-exposure.json` using `sql-nscs-platform-<suffix>`. The optional lightweight database uses `sqldb-customer-index`. Disable or remove the old `Deploy sample database` LCA to avoid duplicate SQL work.
